WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.787
Welcome back to Building
the Daily Checks Workbook.

2
00:00:02.787 --> 00:00:06.825
This is Chapter 2: the workbook's
template, and its validator.

3
00:00:06.825 --> 00:00:10.598
A workbook edited in the portal
is a change nobody reviewed,

4
00:00:10.598 --> 00:00:15.063
so the kit keeps it as a file and
checks every copy against the manifest.

5
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:19.820
We'll start from Microsoft Learn's page on
workbooks as Resource Manager templates,

6
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.922
see what it leaves to you,
read how the template is built

7
00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:26.025
and the ten checks the validator
runs, and walk two labs.

8
00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:29.320
The chapter is a draft
awaiting the owner's review.

9
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.920
Why keep a dashboard as a file?

10
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.001
Because a workbook edited in the portal is
a change nobody reviewed, and an export

11
00:00:40.001 --> 00:00:45.082
of it can carry the subscription, resource
group and workspace into a repository.

12
00:00:45.082 --> 00:00:49.568
By the end of this chapter you can rebuild
the workbook's template from reviewed

13
00:00:49.568 --> 00:00:52.967
files, prove it has one tab per
daily check and no embedded I D's,

14
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:57.657
and catch the portal edits that would
otherwise drift into production unreviewed.

15
00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.326
It's for the developers
and for the security

16
00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.440
operations engineer
who edits the workbook.

17
00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.215
Here's what Microsoft Learn gives you.

18
00:01:09.215 --> 00:01:13.257
Two ways to manage a workbook as a
template: copy the Gallery Template

19
00:01:13.257 --> 00:01:17.015
from the Advanced Editor, or copy
the Resource Manager template.

20
00:01:17.015 --> 00:01:22.077
The instance is a Microsoft dot Insights
workbooks resource, kind shared,

21
00:01:22.077 --> 00:01:24.898
with a display name, a
source I D, a category,

22
00:01:24.898 --> 00:01:28.715
and serialized data, which
holds the workbook's content.

23
00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:32.647
And Learn warns that an exported
template often embeds the

24
00:01:32.647 --> 00:01:36.740
subscription I D and resource
group: its advice is to mask them.

25
00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:41.852
The resource reference gives
API version 2023-06-01.

26
00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:45.550
Queries use the Logs
data source, with K Q L.

27
00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.525
What does it leave to you?

28
00:01:50.525 --> 00:01:53.510
Learn's way is to export
from the portal and paste,

29
00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:58.584
so the template is whatever someone last
saved; the kit builds it from the manifest

30
00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:02.912
and the K Q L files, and a test keeps
the committed file equal to the build.

31
00:02:02.912 --> 00:02:06.739
Masking I D's by hand
misses one sooner or later,

32
00:02:06.739 --> 00:02:11.875
so a check fails any G U I D,
subscription path, address or secret.

33
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:13.297
A query is free text,

34
00:02:13.297 --> 00:02:17.650
so the kit checks each tab's
tables and each query's look-back.

35
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.075
It checks that every query
reads the workspace parameter.

36
00:02:21.075 --> 00:02:25.790
And because nothing says what a tab
means, every tab must carry the banner.

37
00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.540
Here's the code.

38
00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.365
The template has a header with
the banner, then the parameters:

39
00:02:34.365 --> 00:02:38.715
a workspace picker and four text
values, all left empty in the template.

40
00:02:38.715 --> 00:02:40.594
Then one tab per daily check,

41
00:02:40.594 --> 00:02:45.660
and one group per tab that shows when
its tab is selected, holding the banner,

42
00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:50.235
the daily check, what to do, the link-outs
with click paths, the G C C note,

43
00:02:50.235 --> 00:02:54.565
and its queries, each one a Logs
query on the workspace parameter.

44
00:02:54.565 --> 00:03:00.650
The validator runs ten checks: the format,
one tab per check, tables, look-backs,

45
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.224
the workspace, the banner,
link-outs and hosts,

46
00:03:04.224 --> 00:03:09.410
queries per tab kind, the telemetry
list, and no I D's or secrets.

47
00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.085
Who does what?

48
00:03:14.085 --> 00:03:18.352
The security operations engineer
edits a test copy in the portal,

49
00:03:18.352 --> 00:03:20.723
exports it and validates the export.

50
00:03:20.723 --> 00:03:24.635
A second person reviews the change
before it replaces the template.

51
00:03:24.635 --> 00:03:27.622
Developers keep the
manifest and the queries.

52
00:03:27.622 --> 00:03:29.497
Lab 1 needs only files.

53
00:03:29.497 --> 00:03:33.979
Lab 2 saves one test workbook, so it
needs Workbook Contributor on the

54
00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:38.460
test resource group, for the lab only,
and it deletes the copy at the end.

55
00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.620
A reviewer checks that no export
with I D's in it was committed.

56
00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.670
Lab 1, in the kit's
folder, with no tenant.

57
00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.481
Step 1 confirms the
committed template matches

58
00:03:52.481 --> 00:03:54.870
the build of the manifest and the queries.

59
00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.168
Step 2 validates it: ten checks,

60
00:03:57.168 --> 00:04:01.760
sixty-three results across the
tabs, and all of them pass.

61
00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.972
Step 3 is the one to remember.

62
00:04:07.972 --> 00:04:11.948
A copy was exported after someone
edited the workbook in the portal.

63
00:04:11.948 --> 00:04:16.983
Four edits, four failures: one risk query
reads a workspace path instead of the

64
00:04:16.983 --> 00:04:21.861
parameter; the devices query looks back
seven hundred and twenty hours; the

65
00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:26.897
grants tab lost its banner; and the file
carries a G U I D and a subscription path.

66
00:04:26.897 --> 00:04:31.849
Step 4 shows what the export carried:
the workspace's full resource path,

67
00:04:31.849 --> 00:04:35.140
exactly what Microsoft Learn says to mask.

68
00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:44.004
Step 5 records a validation of the kit's
template: the same sixty-three checks pass,

69
00:04:44.004 --> 00:04:47.286
and the results go to a folder
with a hashed manifest,

70
00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.652
ready for Chapter 4's evidence record.

71
00:04:49.652 --> 00:04:54.139
Step 6 runs this chapter's
tests: ten passed, none failed.

72
00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:56.350
Then delete the output folder.

73
00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:05.387
Lab 2 runs in a test subscription, never
production, and the authors haven't run it.

74
00:05:05.387 --> 00:05:09.246
Open the template in the portal
through the Advanced Editor,

75
00:05:09.246 --> 00:05:12.101
pick the test workspace,
and open all ten tabs.

76
00:05:12.101 --> 00:05:17.038
Save a test copy, change one look-back,
and copy the Gallery Template back out.

77
00:05:17.038 --> 00:05:19.457
Validate the export: your edit fails,

78
00:05:19.457 --> 00:05:22.763
and so does the workspace
the portal saved into it.

79
00:05:22.763 --> 00:05:25.987
Record any other difference
the portal introduced;

80
00:05:25.987 --> 00:05:30.562
that confirms the item format, which
Learn doesn't document field by field.

81
00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:33.730
Then delete the test copy and the export.

82
00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:38.655
What does this support?

83
00:05:38.655 --> 00:05:42.365
The build check shows the template
is the reviewed baseline,

84
00:05:42.365 --> 00:05:44.442
configuration management C M two.

85
00:05:44.442 --> 00:05:48.788
The validation record supports C M
two and change control, C M three,

86
00:05:48.788 --> 00:05:53.843
and catching a portal edit before it
replaces the template supports C M three.

87
00:05:53.843 --> 00:05:58.328
The dangers are the four edits you
just saw: an export committed as is,

88
00:05:58.328 --> 00:06:02.893
a widened look-back, a query on another
workspace, and a missing banner.

89
00:06:02.893 --> 00:06:04.080
Each has its check.

90
00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.850
Next, Chapter 3 shows what each tab
would display, without a tenant.
